# Feature areas (#873): which paths belong to which feature, so that two lanes do not
# work on the same feature at the same time. One area can cover App, Remote, Web,
# packages and docs.
#
# Each line is a path pattern and an area. Patterns start at the repository root:
# `*` matches inside one folder, `**` matches across folders, and a pattern that ends
# in `/` matches everything under that folder. The last line that matches a path wins.
# The area `-` means no area: use it for shared files that every lane touches.
#
# The CI step (.github/workflows/areas.yml, scripts/pr-areas.py) gives each pull request
# an `area:<name>` label for each area its changed files are in, and warns when another
# open pull request holds the same area. Add an area when the replay
# (scripts/replay-conflicts.py) shows two lanes conflicting on a feature that has none.

# The broad lines come first, so that the feature lines below them win (#873).

